        "original_id": "810c8edd-95d1-5b72-a531-63848b3657d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robbin Crosby\n- Organizations: Ratt, RIAA\n- Topics: glam metal, heavy metal, Los Angeles glam metal scene, hair metal, pop metal\n\nFacts:\n- Robbinson Lantz Crosby was born on August 4, 1959, and died on June 6, 2002.\n- Robbin Crosby was an American guitarist and a member of Ratt.\n- In the 1980s, Robbin Crosby and Ratt earned several platinum albums in the United States.\n- In the 1980s, Ratt was an American heavy metal band with significant commercial success.\n- Ratt's albums were certified gold, platinum, and multi-platinum by the RIAA.\n- In the early 1980s, Ratt was recognized as instrumental in forming the Los Angeles glam metal scene.\n- The Los Angeles glam metal scene was also known as hair metal or pop metal.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
